    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0254" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1828 <hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >4/7</hi></note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State
                            (White)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-07-29">July 29, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Espil called and told me that a
                    telegram regarding the manifesto which Argentina wanted Brazil, Chile and Peru
                    to join with them was being decoded; that as soon as this was done he would send
                    me a copy,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d156-f1"/> and that in the meantime he had
                    received two other cables, one asking him to try to get the Neutral Commission
                    to urge the Brazilian Government to join with it, and the other stating that the
                    matter of a declaration that the nations of this hemisphere would not recognize
                    any conquest made by Paraguay and Bolivia now appealed very strongly to the
                    Argentine Government, but that it hesitated to take the initiative in making the
                    suggestion unless it knew that Brazil, Chile and Peru, at least, would also join
                    in, feeling that should it be known that Argentina had taken the initiative in
                    the matter and the other countries had not joined them, it would put Argentina
                    in a very difficult position vis-à-vis the Bolivian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
